<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jabrin Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1670</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Jabreen Castle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jabrin Castle is a fortified palace near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahla">Bahla</a> in the interior of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a>, built around 1670 by the Ya'aruba <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> Bil'arab ibn <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a>. Unlike most Omani forts it was designed chiefly as a residence and centre of learning, with painted ceilings, carved woodwork and Arabic inscriptions. Bil'arab was buried there, and it is regarded as one of the finest examples of Omani architecture.</p></div>
